WEBVTT

00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:31.788
And that simply means this is me going.

00:00:32.121 --> 00:00:37.662
Yep. This is Jane Goodall, legendary
ethologist, an expert on primate behavior.

00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:40.871
Jane greeted us from her home
in the U.K. over Zoome.

00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:42.954
It's an unnatural habitat for

00:00:42.954 --> 00:00:45.787
a person who usually spends
most of her time outdoors.

00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:52.621
More than 60 years ago, Jane started her
career studying chimpanzees in Tanzania,

00:00:52.954 --> 00:00:54.787
along with anthropologist Lewis Leakey.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.912
She famously immersed herself
with wild chimps

00:00:57.912 --> 00:01:01.621
and made groundbreaking discoveries about
how primates behave and communicate.